WEBVTT

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:23.050
Before I knew it, I abandoned happiness to survive

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:30.190
Lying to myself, I danced clinging on to illusions

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:36.870
At the edge of my vision when I close my eyes

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:42.840
I was searching for your smile

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:50.210
With our memories fading

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:57.290
We hold on to our dreams and run  Yeah

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:04.190
These feelings that I shut away in my heart

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:11.410
I'll now grasp them again

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:35.180
KC Grand Prix Begins

00:01:52.580 --> 00:01:54.520
Food’s ready!

00:01:56.120 --> 00:01:56.800
Ouch...

00:01:57.360 --> 00:01:59.370
Wake up already.

00:01:59.370 --> 00:02:02.370
Ouch...  What’s with you?

00:02:02.370 --> 00:02:03.650
You scared me.

00:02:03.650 --> 00:02:06.310
How long were you gonna sleep?

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:11.250
I'm tired after all that stuff that happened.

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:14.250
Let us sleep.

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:15.390
Where’s my darling?

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:18.320
He’s not here?

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:20.760
I wonder where he went?

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:38.570
I feel great!

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:41.760
Partner...

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:46.440
It feels like everything that happened was a dream.

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:48.880
My other self...

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:54.740
I'll never forget everyone involved in our recent battle.

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:57.220
Or the world of Duel Monsters.

00:02:57.910 --> 00:03:00.900
And how I hurt you, partner.

00:03:01.970 --> 00:03:03.900
My other self...

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:11.500
When we return to Japan, we can finally unlock your memories.

00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:20.310
I don’t know what'll happen then.

00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:23.260
But no matter what, I’ll never forget.

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:30.690
After meeting you, the good times and the bad times are all special to me.

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:32.620
Partner...

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:36.010
Yugi!

00:03:36.010 --> 00:03:37.000
Darling!

00:03:37.630 --> 00:03:39.390
Here you are.

00:03:39.390 --> 00:03:40.560
Food's ready-

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:42.300
Darling!

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:48.470
If you disappear, I get worried!

00:03:48.470 --> 00:03:51.750
S-Sorry...  I was just taking a walk...

00:03:52.570 --> 00:03:54.280
Everyone’s waiting.

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:56.030
Let’s have breakfast.

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:57.650
Let’s go.

00:03:57.650 --> 00:03:58.520
O-Okay.

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:03.010
You’re late, Yugi!

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:03.540
Sorry!

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:05.390
Let’s eat!

00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:09.420
Delish!

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:14.240
What are you planning to do now?

00:04:15.430 --> 00:04:18.180
It’s about time we go home to Japan.

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:23.360
What's the rush?  Take a break.

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:25.840
That’s right.  You're on vacation.

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:28.520
I can be your tour guide.

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:30.280
That sounds nice!

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:32.410
I mean, we did come to America.

00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:35.100
Yeah!  Let’s eat famous American food!

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:37.200
Like a giant steak or lobster!

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:40.200
You only think about food?

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:42.560
Then what are you gonna do, Anzu?

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:46.020
It’s my phone.

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:53.780
Hello?

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:57.380
Oh, it’s you...  Yes...

00:04:57.920 --> 00:04:59.820
Huh?  What?

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:03.920
Yugi, if we go home now, we’re wasting an opportunity.

00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:05.760
Yeah...  But...

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:10.190
I see.  You want to go home for the other Yugi.

00:05:11.470 --> 00:05:13.360
Oh yeah.

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:21.790
Partner, we retrieved the God Cards.

00:05:21.790 --> 00:05:23.670
We don't need to hurry.

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:27.050
It could be nice to take a detour.

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:29.120
My other self...

00:05:31.820 --> 00:05:33.200
You're right.

00:05:33.790 --> 00:05:36.200
We came all this way, so let's have fun!

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:37.160
All right!

00:05:37.160 --> 00:05:39.210
Yeah!  That's the spirit!

00:05:39.210 --> 00:05:39.960
Let's go where?

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:41.470
Hmm...

00:05:41.890 --> 00:05:43.690
Huh?  Where’s the professor?

00:05:43.690 --> 00:05:45.840
He had to leave for a sec.

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:49.760
I recommend going to a theme park.

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:50.560
R-Right.

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:52.200
Let’s get steak!

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:54.980
Let’s go to a wild west show!

00:05:54.980 --> 00:05:56.670
But steak first!

00:05:56.670 --> 00:05:58.470
How long can you stay?

00:05:58.470 --> 00:06:00.510
When's your flight?

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:04.130
What’s wrong?

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:07.810
Oh yeah...  How are we going to get home?

00:06:09.450 --> 00:06:13.210
That’s right.  We came here on Pegasus’s plane.

00:06:13.210 --> 00:06:15.620
We didn’t think about how to get home!

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:17.330
What are we going to do?

00:06:17.330 --> 00:06:19.160
How much does a plane ticket cost?

00:06:19.160 --> 00:06:21.270
I don’t have any money.

00:06:21.270 --> 00:06:22.070
Me neither.

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:25.880
Then stay here forever, darling!

00:06:26.180 --> 00:06:27.030
What?

00:06:27.030 --> 00:06:29.740
He can't!  He’ll miss school!

00:06:31.330 --> 00:06:33.480
Kaiba Corporation?

00:06:37.690 --> 00:06:41.450
Oh.  I can take care of that.

00:06:41.450 --> 00:06:43.200
Really, Mokuba?

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:46.780
I’ll take you home in Kaiba Corporation’s private jet.

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:48.170
Really?

00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:50.020
Wow!  You’re a savior!

00:06:50.020 --> 00:06:50.550
However!

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:54.920
In exchange, you must enter Kaiba Corporation's KC Grand Prix.

00:06:54.920 --> 00:06:58.730
A tournament to determine the greatest duelist.

00:06:59.380 --> 00:07:01.170
Tournament?

00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:04.600
Why a duel tournament?

00:07:04.600 --> 00:07:08.400
You know we’re building a Kaiba Land in America, right?

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:10.400
Yeah.  It was on the news.

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:12.290
They said it’s almost ready.

00:07:12.290 --> 00:07:13.290
That’s right.

00:07:13.290 --> 00:07:18.740
To commemorate its completion, we’re holding a huge duel tournament.

00:07:19.850 --> 00:07:21.970
I'm sorry, Mr. Kaiba.

00:07:21.970 --> 00:07:24.650
We're doing our best, but...

00:07:24.650 --> 00:07:27.100
I’m tired of hearing the same answer.

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:30.040
I’m telling you to get results.

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:33.720
Big brother.

00:07:34.160 --> 00:07:38.020
You got back all the stock that Doma bought, right?

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:45.270
Yeah.  But faith in Kaiba Corporation dropped, lowering the stock price.

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:47.720
How annoying.

00:07:47.720 --> 00:07:54.650
But when the tournament starts, everyone will focus on Kaiba Corporation again.

00:07:55.010 --> 00:07:57.660
And all the bad talk will go away.

00:07:57.660 --> 00:07:58.920
You're right.

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:02.030
Isono, how are the online entrants?

00:08:02.030 --> 00:08:08.470
Completed.  But shouldn’t we ask them to enter too?

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:13.950
Of course.  I owe them this time.

00:08:13.950 --> 00:08:15.840
Then I'll arrange it.

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:17.610
Isono, I’m going too.

00:08:18.140 --> 00:08:19.220
Mokuba...

00:08:19.620 --> 00:08:21.820
Leave it to me, big brother!

00:08:21.820 --> 00:08:24.480
I’ll make them show up!

00:08:27.500 --> 00:08:30.890
And that’s why I came to get you.

00:08:31.260 --> 00:08:33.160
Wait a second!

00:08:33.160 --> 00:08:35.770
You entered us without our permission!

00:08:35.770 --> 00:08:39.850
Kaiba himself should come and beg us to enter!

00:08:39.850 --> 00:08:44.980
Yeah.  Because this is like a commercial for Kaiba Corporation.

00:08:44.980 --> 00:08:49.980
Yugi and Jonouchi did well in Battle City, so it'll be news if they enter.

00:08:49.980 --> 00:08:53.230
My brother is busy!

00:08:53.230 --> 00:08:58.880
As the organizer of this tournament, he's so busy that he can't compete!

00:08:58.880 --> 00:09:02.140
What?  Kaiba isn't going to duel?

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:04.400
He must be really busy.

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:06.730
I get it.

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:11.230
He’s afraid he'll lose to me or Yugi.

00:09:11.230 --> 00:09:15.400
If he loses again, Kaiba Corporation’s reputation will plummet.

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:17.860
My brother will never lose!

00:09:17.860 --> 00:09:24.970
He's prioritizing his work as the company's president than being a duelist!

00:09:24.970 --> 00:09:29.010
To realize our dream of creating Kaiba Land...

00:09:29.010 --> 00:09:30.800
Mokuba...

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:32.960
Jonouchi, you went too far.

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:38.160
Okay, I understand it's a lot of work.

00:09:38.520 --> 00:09:43.370
Yugi, Kaiba Corporation is risking everything for this tournament.

00:09:43.970 --> 00:09:50.670
We chose the best duelists from around the world to get the people excited.

00:09:52.290 --> 00:09:54.500
That’s why I want you to enter!

00:09:54.500 --> 00:09:55.970
As the Duel King!

00:10:02.690 --> 00:10:06.430
The world’s greatest duelists?  Sounds fun!

00:10:06.430 --> 00:10:08.420
And I'll get to have fun duels.

00:10:09.530 --> 00:10:12.740
So you’ll participate?  Thanks, Yugi!

00:10:12.740 --> 00:10:14.810
If Yugi’s entering, so am I!

00:10:15.530 --> 00:10:16.960
Me too!

00:10:16.960 --> 00:10:20.270
As the U.S. champ, I have the qualifications!

00:10:20.270 --> 00:10:22.990
Darling, let’s enter together!

00:10:22.990 --> 00:10:23.900
R-Right...

00:10:23.900 --> 00:10:28.340
That’s what I planned from the start, so I brought you all invitations.

00:10:30.100 --> 00:10:32.800
Do the best duels!

00:10:33.150 --> 00:10:35.920
Leave it to us.  Right, Yugi?

00:10:35.920 --> 00:10:38.910
Now there’s no doubt it’ll be a huge success!

00:10:58.420 --> 00:11:01.760
Master Sieg, you have mail.

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:02.720
Okay.

00:11:17.220 --> 00:11:19.080
KC Grand Prix.

00:11:23.300 --> 00:11:25.420
You don’t know yet.

00:11:25.980 --> 00:11:31.380
Seto Kaiba, you’re using this event to restore Kaiba Corporation.

00:11:31.380 --> 00:11:34.300
But instead, it'll end you.

00:11:59.080 --> 00:12:02.070
This Is Kaiba Land USA.

00:12:03.290 --> 00:12:05.490
It's huge!

00:12:05.490 --> 00:12:07.940
There are lots of rides.

00:12:07.940 --> 00:12:11.520
It has the most rides in the world!

00:12:11.900 --> 00:12:14.490
Seems fun!  Right, Yugi?

00:12:14.490 --> 00:12:15.300
Yeah!

00:12:15.300 --> 00:12:18.380
When it opens, let’s come here on a date, darling!

00:12:18.890 --> 00:12:22.330
Sheesh.  I want to date Yugi too.

00:12:32.020 --> 00:12:34.440
You must've spent a lot of money!

00:12:34.440 --> 00:12:37.880
This is the main gate.  The shopping arcade is inside.

00:12:42.220 --> 00:12:43.570
I knew he'd have this.

00:12:44.540 --> 00:12:46.980
What are you doing, Jonouchi?

00:12:50.770 --> 00:12:52.170
Hey, Mokuba.

00:12:52.170 --> 00:12:53.290
What?

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:57.680
You invited skilled duelists for this tournament, right?

00:12:57.680 --> 00:13:00.130
Yeah.  From around the world.

00:13:00.130 --> 00:13:05.330
Does that mean you invited Mai Kujaku?

00:13:05.330 --> 00:13:11.660
Well...  She was on the invite list, but we don’t know where she is.

00:13:11.660 --> 00:13:12.770
I see.

00:13:13.340 --> 00:13:14.700
Jonouchi...

00:13:15.140 --> 00:13:19.140
Knowing her, she’s happily dueling somewhere.

00:13:19.140 --> 00:13:21.240
You're right.

00:13:28.110 --> 00:13:30.810
People are already here?

00:13:30.810 --> 00:13:33.500
Special guests before the official opening.

00:13:34.580 --> 00:13:37.090
You can also ride anything you want later.

00:13:37.590 --> 00:13:38.690
Really?

00:13:38.690 --> 00:13:42.200
All right!  Let's ride all the scream machines!

00:13:42.200 --> 00:13:43.100
Yeah!

00:13:43.520 --> 00:13:45.110
You guys are such kids...

00:13:45.110 --> 00:13:49.970
The tournament finals will be held in this duel stadium.

00:13:51.450 --> 00:13:53.570
A Blue-Eyes dome...

00:13:53.570 --> 00:13:55.990
Isn't this going too far?

00:13:55.990 --> 00:13:56.920
Right?

00:13:58.040 --> 00:14:00.360
That’s the main duel stage.

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:04.290
The duel will be broadcast worldwide.

00:14:04.290 --> 00:14:05.890
Worldwide?

00:14:05.890 --> 00:14:09.210
So don't have an embarrassing duel.

00:14:09.210 --> 00:14:09.730
What?

00:14:10.180 --> 00:14:12.660
Gagagigo attacks Blade Knight!

00:14:16.530 --> 00:14:17.930
All right!

00:14:17.930 --> 00:14:21.310
Activating Quick-Play Spell, Scapegoat.

00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:26.710
Why are you using Scapegoat now?

00:14:26.710 --> 00:14:28.850
I'm ending my turn.

00:14:28.850 --> 00:14:30.900
What’s up with that computer?

00:14:30.900 --> 00:14:32.840
Can it duel properly?

00:14:32.840 --> 00:14:34.140
Just watch.

00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:37.440
The set card's identity is the key.

00:14:38.160 --> 00:14:39.620
My turn.

00:14:39.620 --> 00:14:44.060
Activating trap card, DNA Surgery.

00:14:44.060 --> 00:14:50.660
As long as it's on the field, all monsters on the field change to a Type of my choice.

00:14:50.660 --> 00:14:52.090
No way!

00:14:52.090 --> 00:14:55.040
I choose Dragon-Type.

00:14:56.230 --> 00:14:58.080
Even my Gagagigo?

00:15:02.690 --> 00:15:07.120
Then I activate the spell card, Polymerization from my hand.

00:15:07.390 --> 00:15:09.460
It's fusing all its monsters together?

00:15:09.460 --> 00:15:10.290
No way!

00:15:10.290 --> 00:15:16.790
I fuse my five Dragon-Type monsters to summon Five-Headed Dragon.

00:15:21.990 --> 00:15:24.370
You must be joking!

00:15:24.800 --> 00:15:27.670
Five-Headed Dragon has 5000 attack points!

00:15:27.670 --> 00:15:29.280
Seriously?

00:15:29.280 --> 00:15:32.160
A computer uses monsters like that?

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:33.850
Surprised?

00:15:33.850 --> 00:15:39.780
This Duel Computer is programmed with many duelist and card data.

00:15:40.180 --> 00:15:44.450
Including my brother's, Yugi's and Jonouchi’s data.

00:15:44.450 --> 00:15:46.170
What?  Mine too?

00:15:46.170 --> 00:15:49.490
Jonouchi’s data?  But he only uses luck-

00:15:49.490 --> 00:15:51.200
Say what!

00:15:51.200 --> 00:15:55.300
But if it’s such a strong computer, no one can put up a fight.

00:15:55.300 --> 00:15:56.900
Don't worry.

00:15:56.900 --> 00:16:01.840
You can select the level of difficulty, so even novices can have fun.

00:16:01.840 --> 00:16:04.840
This is one of Kaiba Land's main attractions.

00:16:04.840 --> 00:16:06.140
How fun!

00:16:06.140 --> 00:16:10.000
With this, you can even duel against yourself.

00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:10.850
That’s true.

00:16:11.880 --> 00:16:13.980
Five-Headed Dragon attacks.

00:16:17.790 --> 00:16:20.520
Aww, I lost.

00:16:20.520 --> 00:16:23.530
I told you that you set the level too high.

00:16:23.530 --> 00:16:24.960
It’s my turn.

00:16:25.250 --> 00:16:27.320
You did pretty well.

00:16:27.320 --> 00:16:29.470
If you make your deck a little stronger-

00:16:29.470 --> 00:16:32.150
Hey!  It’s Yugi Muto, the Duel King!

00:16:32.710 --> 00:16:34.190
You’re right!

00:16:34.190 --> 00:16:35.840
Wow!  Is it really him?

00:16:35.840 --> 00:16:38.200
Also the American champ, Rebecca!

00:16:38.200 --> 00:16:39.140
Autograph please!

00:16:39.140 --> 00:16:39.870
Me too!

00:16:40.930 --> 00:16:43.780
Wow, Yugi.  You’re famous.

00:16:43.780 --> 00:16:45.710
R-Really?

00:16:46.720 --> 00:16:48.710
I’m Leon.

00:16:48.710 --> 00:16:51.680
I’ve watched your duels.  I'm a big fan!

00:16:51.680 --> 00:16:54.160
I’m happy to meet you!

00:16:54.740 --> 00:16:56.040
Thank you!

00:16:56.040 --> 00:16:58.250
How about my autograph?

00:16:58.250 --> 00:16:59.670
I don’t want it.

00:16:59.670 --> 00:17:00.800
Who are you?

00:17:00.800 --> 00:17:05.100
Katsuya Jonouchi!  I was in the Top 4 at Battle City!

00:17:05.100 --> 00:17:06.350
No clue.

00:17:06.740 --> 00:17:09.030
Too bad, Jonouchi.

00:17:09.740 --> 00:17:11.180
Why...

00:17:11.180 --> 00:17:14.910
Umm, can you look at my deck?

00:17:14.910 --> 00:17:16.000
Your deck?

00:17:16.000 --> 00:17:17.750
I always lose.

00:17:17.750 --> 00:17:21.200
What can I do to be strong like you, Yugi?

00:17:22.650 --> 00:17:24.190
What's with that?

00:17:24.190 --> 00:17:26.230
It’s full of Dragon-Type monsters.

00:17:26.230 --> 00:17:28.190
I like dragons.

00:17:28.190 --> 00:17:31.110
So I traded with my friends to get lots of them.

00:17:32.290 --> 00:17:36.660
I understand that you like them, but your deck's balance isn’t good.

00:17:36.660 --> 00:17:38.360
What?  It’s no good?

00:17:38.360 --> 00:17:40.810
That’s not what I mean...

00:17:40.810 --> 00:17:45.970
Don’t worry.  Your love towards your cards will make your cards stronger!

00:17:46.590 --> 00:17:50.030
And your cards will respond in kind.

00:17:50.030 --> 00:17:50.920
Really?

00:17:52.300 --> 00:17:53.580
Oh yeah!

00:17:54.250 --> 00:17:55.380
I’ll give you this.

00:17:55.380 --> 00:17:56.720
Really?

00:17:56.720 --> 00:17:57.390
Yeah.

00:17:59.290 --> 00:18:01.660
Huh?  It’s not a dragon.

00:18:01.660 --> 00:18:05.730
But that card will help your dragons.

00:18:05.730 --> 00:18:06.830
Really?

00:18:07.830 --> 00:18:09.380
You're so lucky!

00:18:09.380 --> 00:18:10.720
I want one too!

00:18:10.720 --> 00:18:13.010
Yugi, what card was that?

00:18:13.010 --> 00:18:14.730
Well...  Uh...

00:18:15.680 --> 00:18:18.210
I’ll use it to duel!

00:18:18.760 --> 00:18:20.210
Good luck!

00:18:20.210 --> 00:18:22.680
You shouldn’t raise the level too high!

00:18:23.120 --> 00:18:25.590
Umm...  In that case...

00:18:25.590 --> 00:18:27.440
I’ll try level 2!

00:18:33.860 --> 00:18:36.300
Let me introduce myself.

00:18:47.810 --> 00:18:48.780
Duel!

00:18:52.370 --> 00:18:54.230
A blackout?

00:18:55.510 --> 00:18:57.930
To be safe, don't move!

00:18:57.930 --> 00:18:59.920
Mokuba, what’s going on?

00:19:00.370 --> 00:19:02.480
How weird.  This shouldn't happen.

00:19:02.900 --> 00:19:04.830
It's still a trial run, right?

00:19:04.830 --> 00:19:06.850
Maybe it's a glitch.

00:19:07.320 --> 00:19:09.140
Everyone, stay calm.

00:19:09.140 --> 00:19:10.880
It’ll be fixed shortly.

00:19:13.220 --> 00:19:14.160
The lights are on.

00:19:16.970 --> 00:19:17.670
What?

00:19:22.040 --> 00:19:23.280
What’s going on?

00:19:23.280 --> 00:19:25.560
Why did the emergency shutters close?

00:19:25.560 --> 00:19:27.130
They won’t open!

00:19:27.130 --> 00:19:28.550
How could this be?

00:19:29.070 --> 00:19:30.420
Let me try.

00:19:33.640 --> 00:19:34.890
How goes it?

00:19:34.890 --> 00:19:36.450
No good.

00:19:36.450 --> 00:19:42.130
The program’s been locked, and all systems are connected to the Duel Computer.

00:19:42.740 --> 00:19:46.570
Unless the Duel Computer is shut down, the exits won’t open.

00:19:46.570 --> 00:19:49.560
This shouldn't happen!

00:19:49.560 --> 00:19:52.000
That computer is only for dueling!

00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:54.510
It has nothing to do with the control system!

00:19:54.930 --> 00:19:58.870
Someone hacked in and rewrote the program.

00:19:58.870 --> 00:19:59.680
What?

00:20:00.140 --> 00:20:02.470
Who’s doing that?

00:20:02.470 --> 00:20:03.980
I don’t know.

00:20:03.980 --> 00:20:06.980
Why don’t we just destroy the computer?

00:20:06.980 --> 00:20:08.650
I’ll do it!

00:20:08.650 --> 00:20:13.100
Wait!  If you do that, we might never be able to get out!

00:20:13.100 --> 00:20:14.920
Then what should we do?

00:20:15.500 --> 00:20:19.330
If you defeat the Duel Computer, the locks will open.

00:20:19.330 --> 00:20:23.650
So we can’t get out unless we win the duel.

00:20:24.610 --> 00:20:25.800
Oh no!

00:20:25.800 --> 00:20:28.140
Huh?  What do you mean?

00:20:28.140 --> 00:20:29.530
Duel start.

00:20:29.530 --> 00:20:30.740
My turn.

00:20:30.740 --> 00:20:34.370
I summon Berserk Gorilla in attack position.

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:38.680
I set one card and end my turn.

00:20:39.220 --> 00:20:41.680
He has to duel?  What's the level?

00:20:41.680 --> 00:20:43.080
Look!

00:20:43.080 --> 00:20:45.480
That’s the max level!

00:20:45.480 --> 00:20:48.050
Can this kid win?

00:20:48.050 --> 00:20:50.360
I’m scared!

00:20:50.360 --> 00:20:51.990
There's no way he can win!

00:20:51.990 --> 00:20:54.350
The deck is already set!

00:20:54.350 --> 00:20:55.840
He can’t change it!

00:20:55.840 --> 00:20:56.910
What?

00:20:56.910 --> 00:20:59.980
It’s a badly-balanced deck full of dragons!

00:20:59.980 --> 00:21:03.650
He can't win on the highest level setting!

00:21:04.440 --> 00:21:05.950
My other self...

00:21:13.190 --> 00:21:14.410
Yugi!

00:21:14.940 --> 00:21:17.420
Calm down.  I’m by your side.

00:21:18.810 --> 00:21:20.370
What’s your name?

00:21:20.370 --> 00:21:21.530
Rick.

00:21:21.530 --> 00:21:26.460
Rick, let me use your precious deck.

00:21:27.730 --> 00:21:29.130
Okay!

00:21:29.130 --> 00:21:31.600
Yugi!

00:21:31.600 --> 00:21:33.710
Darling!  Do your best!

00:21:33.710 --> 00:21:35.010
I’m counting on you, Yugi.

00:21:35.760 --> 00:21:37.170
I’m your opponent!

00:21:39.600 --> 00:21:42.550
I'll free everyone from here!

00:21:56.340 --> 00:22:05.220
The streets flow by, colored in red

00:22:05.750 --> 00:22:13.590
If you notice your pain, it changes to joy

00:22:15.320 --> 00:22:24.750
People learn of friendship every time they wipe their tears

00:22:25.360 --> 00:22:34.240
With the warm strength you gave me, I'll change them into kindness

00:22:34.840 --> 00:22:43.300
My overflowing emotions don't stop

00:22:44.080 --> 00:22:48.810
I'll live feeling them

00:22:49.420 --> 00:22:53.960
For me to be me

00:22:53.960 --> 00:23:02.450
Overflowing friendship heals me

00:23:03.130 --> 00:23:08.090
Our chance meeting was real

00:23:08.610 --> 00:23:17.750
We'll both understand that someday

00:23:24.340 --> 00:23:27.810
KC Grand Prix seems fun!

00:23:27.810 --> 00:23:35.260
We happily came to Kaiba Land, but someone trapped us inside a dome.

00:23:35.260 --> 00:23:38.620
We can't escape unless we defeat the computer in a duel.

00:23:38.620 --> 00:23:43.370
But the opponent's level is at max, and we're using a badly-balanced deck full of dragons.

00:23:43.370 --> 00:23:45.660
Can you really win, Yugi?

00:23:46.260 --> 00:23:49.060
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
The Scheme Begins

00:23:49.060 --> 00:23:50.600
Duel, standby!
